<h1>Amazon Bedrock for LLMs <span class="accent">Deep Dive</span></h1>
<p class="hero-sub">Model access, InvokeModel API, streaming, knowledge bases, and agent architectures</p>
</section>
<div class="objectives"><h4>Learning Objectives</h4><ul><li>Access and provision foundation models through Bedrock</li><li>Implement InvokeModel API patterns with request/response handling</li><li>Build streaming inference pipelines for real-time applications</li><li>Integrate knowledge bases and RAG with Bedrock agents</li><li>Design multi-model agent systems with tool calling</li></ul></div>

<section class="section" id="overview">
<h2>Overview</h2>
<p>Amazon Bedrock provides serverless access to foundation models from AWS, Anthropic, Meta, and third-party providers. Unlike managing infrastructure or using APIs directly, Bedrock handles scaling, security, and model versions automatically. This lesson covers practical patterns for accessing models, building intelligent agents with memory and tools, and integrating knowledge bases for retrieval-augmented generation.</p>

<p>Bedrock's model access layer abstracts away deployment complexity while maintaining fine-grained control over prompts, parameters, and costs. You'll learn how to architect solutions that leverage multiple models, handle streaming responses efficiently, and build agents that can reason over custom knowledge.</p>
</section>

<section class="section" id="model-access">
<h2>Model Access and Provisioning</h2>

<p>Bedrock models are provisioned through the AWS console or programmatically. Each model has a specific invocation format and parameter constraints. Understanding these nuances prevents common integration errors.</p>

<div class="infographic">
  <strong>Bedrock Model Landscape</strong><br><br>
  AWS: Titan (base, express, premier) | Anthropic: Claude 1-3, Haiku | Meta: Llama 2, 3 | Google: PaLM 2<br>
  Vision models available for image understanding | Text embedding models for RAG<br>
  Each model: different pricing, context windows, capabilities
</div>

<p><strong>Model Request Syntax</strong>: Bedrock abstracts differences between providers using a unified API. However, each model's system prompt handling, parameter names, and response formats vary subtly.</p>

<div class="code"><span class="im">import</span> <span class="nm">boto3</span><span class="op">,</span> <span class="nm">json</span><br><span class="kw">from</span> <span class="nm">botocore</span>.<span class="nm">exceptions</span> <span class="kw">import</span> <span class="nm">ClientError</span><br><br><span class="nm">client</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">boto3</span>.<span class="fn">client</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="st">'bedrock-runtime'</span><span class="op">)</span><br><br><span class="cm"># Invoke Claude 3 Sonnet</span><br><span class="nm">response</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">client</span>.<span class="fn">invoke_model</span><span class="op">(</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">modelId</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">'anthropic.claude-3-sonnet-20240229-v1:0'</span><span class="op">,</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">body</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">json</span>.<span class="fn">dumps</span><span class="op">({</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'anthropic_version'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">'bedrock-2023-06-01'</span><span class="op">,</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'max_tokens'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="nm">1024</span><span class="op">,</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'messages'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="op">[{</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'role'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">'user'</span><span class="op">,</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'content'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">'Explain quantum entanglement'</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="op">}]</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="op">})</span><br><span class="op">)</span><br><br><span class="nm">result</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">json</span>.<span class="fn">loads</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="nm">response</span><span class="op">[</span><span class="st">'body'</span><span class="op">].</span><span class="fn">read</span><span class="op">())</span><br><span class="nm">text</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">result</span><span class="op">[</span><span class="st">'content'</span><span class="op">][</span><span class="nm">0</span><span class="op">][</span><span class="st">'text'</span><span class="op">]</span></div>

<p><strong>Provisioning Through-Put</strong>: For high-traffic applications, enable provisioned throughput to lock in pricing and guarantee availability. This is critical when SLA requirements demand consistent latency.</p>

<div class="callout">
<strong>Provisioned vs On-Demand:</strong> On-demand pays per token, scales elastically. Provisioned throughput offers 50% cost reduction with reserved capacity. Use provisioned for stable, predictable workloads exceeding 3M tokens/month.
</div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="invoke-model">
<h2>InvokeModel API and Request Patterns</h2>

<p>The InvokeModel API is the core interface for synchronous model calls. Each model requires different request payloads. Learning to construct these properly is fundamental.</p>

<div class="code"><span class="cm"># Multi-model adapter pattern</span><br><span class="kw">class</span> <span class="nm">BedrockAdapter</span><span class="op">:</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">__init__</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="va">self</span><span class="op">):</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="va">self</span>.<span class="nm">client</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">boto3</span>.<span class="fn">client</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="st">'bedrock-runtime'</span><span class="op">)</span><br><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">invoke_claude</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="va">self</span><span class="op">,</span> <span class="va">messages</span><span class="op">,</span> <span class="va">system</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">''</span><span class="op">):</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">payload</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="op">{</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'anthropic_version'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">'bedrock-2023-06-01'</span><span class="op">,</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'max_tokens'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="nm">2048</span><span class="op">,</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'temperature'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="nm">0.7</span><span class="op">,</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'messages'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="va">messages</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="op">}</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="kw">if</span> <span class="va">system</span><span class="op">:</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">payload</span><span class="op">[</span><span class="st">'system'</span><span class="op">]</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">system</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">response</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="nm">client</span>.<span class="fn">invoke_model</span><span class="op">(</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">modelId</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">'anthropic.claude-3-sonnet-20240229-v1:0'</span><span class="op">,</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">body</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">json</span>.<span class="fn">dumps</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="nm">payload</span><span class="op">)</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="op">)</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="kw">return</span> <span class="nm">json</span>.<span class="fn">loads</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="nm">response</span><span class="op">[</span><span class="st">'body'</span><span class="op">].</span><span class="fn">read</span><span class="op">())</span><br><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">invoke_llama</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="va">self</span><span class="op">,</span> <span class="va">prompt</span><span class="op">):</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">payload</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="op">{</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'prompt'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="va">prompt</span><span class="op">,</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'max_gen_len'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="nm">512</span><span class="op">,</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'temperature'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="nm">0.8</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="op">}</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">response</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="nm">client</span>.<span class="fn">invoke_model</span><span class="op">(</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">modelId</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">'meta.llama2-70b-chat-v1'</span><span class="op">,</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">body</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">json</span>.<span class="fn">dumps</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="nm">payload</span><span class="op">)</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="op">)</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="kw">return</span> <span class="nm">json</span>.<span class="fn">loads</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="nm">response</span><span class="op">[</span><span class="st">'body'</span><span class="op">].</span><span class="fn">read</span><span class="op">())</span></div>

<div class="callout warning">
<strong>Error Handling:</strong> Bedrock can throttle requests exceeding provisioned throughput. Implement exponential backoff for rate limiting (429 errors) and circuit breaker patterns for unavailable models.
</div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="streaming">
<h2>Streaming and Real-Time Inference</h2>

<p>Streaming responses enable progressive generation and immediate user feedback. This is critical for conversational AI where token-level latency matters.</p>

<div class="code"><span class="cm"># Streaming response pattern</span><br><span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">stream_bedrock_response</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="va">messages</span><span class="op">,</span> <span class="va">system</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">''</span><span class="op">):</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">client</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">boto3</span>.<span class="fn">client</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="st">'bedrock-runtime'</span><span class="op">)</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">payload</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="op">{</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'anthropic_version'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">'bedrock-2023-06-01'</span><span class="op">,</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'max_tokens'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="nm">2048</span><span class="op">,</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'messages'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="va">messages</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="op">}</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="kw">if</span> <span class="va">system</span><span class="op">:</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">payload</span><span class="op">[</span><span class="st">'system'</span><span class="op">]</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">system</span><br><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">response</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">client</span>.<span class="fn">invoke_model_with_response_stream</span><span class="op">(</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">modelId</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">'anthropic.claude-3-sonnet-20240229-v1:0'</span><span class="op">,</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">body</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">json</span>.<span class="fn">dumps</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="nm">payload</span><span class="op">)</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="op">)</span><br><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="kw">for</span> <span class="nm">event</span> <span class="kw">in</span> <span class="nm">response</span><span class="op">[</span><span class="st">'body'</span><span class="op">]:</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">chunk</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">json</span>.<span class="fn">loads</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="nm">event</span><span class="op">[</span><span class="st">'chunk'</span><span class="op">][</span><span class="st">'bytes'</span><span class="op">])</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="kw">if</span> <span class="st">'content_block_delta'</span> <span class="kw">in</span> <span class="nm">chunk</span><span class="op">:</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">text</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">chunk</span><span class="op">[</span><span class="st">'content_block_delta'</span><span class="op">][</span><span class="st">'delta'</span><span class="op">][</span><span class="st">'text'</span><span class="op">]</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="kw">yield</span> <span class="nm">text</span></div>

<div class="infographic">
  <strong>Streaming Architecture</strong><br><br>
  User Request → Bedrock Streaming API → Event Stream (200ms latency) → WebSocket/SSE to Client<br>
  Buffering: Optional 50-100ms batching for efficiency | Token counting in real-time
</div>

<p>Streaming requires careful error handling. Network disconnects mid-stream must gracefully resume or restart. Consider implementing server-sent events (SSE) for web applications.</p>
</section>

<section class="section" id="knowledge-bases">
<h2>Knowledge Bases and RAG Integration</h2>

<p>Bedrock Knowledge Bases enable RAG without managing vector databases. The service handles embedding, chunking, and retrieval automatically. Integration with agents enables retrieval-augmented reasoning.</p>

<div class="code"><span class="cm"># Knowledge base retrieval with Bedrock</span><br><span class="nm">kb_client</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">boto3</span>.<span class="fn">client</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="st">'bedrock-agent-runtime'</span><span class="op">)</span><br><br><span class="nm">response</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">kb_client</span>.<span class="fn">retrieve</span><span class="op">(</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">knowledgeBaseId</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">'KB_ID'</span><span class="op">,</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">retrievalConfiguration</span><span class="op">={</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'vectorSearchConfiguration'</span><span class="op">:{</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'numberOfResults'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="nm">5</span><span class="op">,</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'overrideSearchType'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">'HYBRID'</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="op">}</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="op">},</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">text</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">'What are our Q3 financial targets?'</span><br><span class="op">)</span><br><br><span class="kw">for</span> <span class="nm">result</span> <span class="kw">in</span> <span class="nm">response</span><span class="op">[</span><span class="st">'retrievalResults'</span><span class="op">]:</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">content</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">result</span><span class="op">[</span><span class="st">'content'</span><span class="op">][</span><span class="st">'text'</span><span class="op">]</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">score</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">result</span><span class="op">[</span><span class="st">'score'</span><span class="op">]</span></div>

<div class="callout success">
<strong>Hybrid Search:</strong> Bedrock supports hybrid retrieval combining keyword matching with semantic search. Use this to balance recall (keyword) with relevance (semantic).
</div>

<p>Knowledge bases support data sources from S3, web crawls, or Salesforce connectors. Synchronization is automatic when source documents change. This eliminates manual vector DB maintenance.</p>
</section>

<section class="section" id="agents">
<h2>Building Intelligent Agents with Tool Calling</h2>

<p>Bedrock Agents enable autonomous reasoning with access to tools and knowledge bases. The agent handles planning, tool selection, and error recovery automatically.</p>

<div class="code"><span class="cm"># Agent with tool definitions</span><br><span class="nm">tools</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="op">[{</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'name'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">'get_customer_orders'</span><span class="op">,</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'description'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">'Retrieve order history for a customer'</span><span class="op">,</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'inputSchema'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="op">{</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'type'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">'object'</span><span class="op">,</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'properties'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="op">{</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'customer_id'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="op">{</span><span class="st">'type'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">'string'</span><span class="op">}</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'limit'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="op">{</span><span class="st">'type'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">'integer'</span><span class="op">,</span> <span class="st">'default'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="nm">10</span><span class="op">}</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="op">}</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="op">}</span><br><span class="op">},{</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'name'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">'update_inventory'</span><span class="op">,</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'description'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">'Update product inventory count'</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'inputSchema'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="op">{</span><span class="st">'type'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">'object'</span><span class="op">,</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'properties'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="op">{</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'product_id'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="op">{</span><span class="st">'type'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">'string'</span><span class="op">}</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="st">'quantity'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="op">{</span><span class="st">'type'</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">'integer'</span><span class="op">}</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="op">}</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="op">}</span><br><span class="op">}]</span><br><br><span class="cm"># Execute agent with message</span><br><span class="nm">agent_response</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">kb_client</span>.<span class="fn">invoke_agent</span><span class="op">(</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">agentId</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">'AGENT_ID'</span><span class="op">,</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">agentAliasId</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">'ALIAS_ID'</span><span class="op">,</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">sessionId</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">'session123'</span><span class="op">,</span><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="nm">inputText</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">'What did customer C123 order in the last 30 days?'</span><br><span class="op">)</span></div>

<div class="infographic">
  <strong>Agent Reasoning Loop</strong><br><br>
  User Message → Agent Analyzes → Selects Tool/Knowledge Base<br>
  → Executes Action → Processes Result → Reasons → Final Response
</div>

<p>Agents maintain session memory and handle multi-step reasoning. Configure action groups to control which tools agents can access and implement approval gates for sensitive operations.</p>
</section>

<section class="section" id="best-practices">
<h2>Production Patterns and Best Practices</h2>

<p><strong>Cost Optimization</strong>: Use smaller models (Haiku) for simple tasks. Batch requests when latency isn't critical. Monitor token usage with CloudWatch metrics.</p>

<p><strong>Error Handling</strong>: Implement exponential backoff for throttling. Log all model invocations for audit trails. Add circuit breakers to prevent cascading failures.</p>

<p><strong>Security</strong>: Use IAM roles with least privilege. Enable content filters for sensitive domains. Encrypt knowledge base documents at rest.</p>

<p><strong>Monitoring</strong>: Track latency, tokens/second, error rates, and cost per transaction. Set up alarms for elevated latency indicating model overload.</p>

<div class="callout success">
<strong>Multi-Model Evaluation:</strong> Run requests against multiple models to evaluate trade-offs. Use Claude for complex reasoning, Haiku for speed, and Llama for specific domains.
</div>
</section>

